@copilot Update this PR directly with a focused correction to instrumentation/vaadin-14.2/javaagent/build.gradle.kts. Preserve all six consolidated testing.suites blocks and the other delivered cleanup. Address the actionable finding in review 5746490820, comment 4450290879: vaadinLatestTest now calls executions unconditionally solely to assign vaadinBuildService. TestSuiteExecutions.kt lines 90-98 automatically attach the default task to check whenever the suite is realized, even with no variants, so unselected-suite realization can widen baseline check coverage.

Restore the existing selection contract: baseline check selects vaadin142Test and vaadin142TestControllerTelemetry; latest-dependency check selects vaadin14LatestTest and vaadinLatestTest plus their ControllerTelemetry variants. Do not attach an unselected suite to check merely to configure its build service. Keep the entire vaadinLatestTest executions declaration conditional on otelProps.testLatestDeps, and preserve usesService(vaadinBuildService) on both the default latest task and its controller variant. Manual vaadinLatestTest runs in baseline mode must still use that service. A single shared tasks.withType<Test>().configureEach with the original name-prefix predicate is acceptable for this genuinely cross-task scheduling constraint; do not invoke executions unconditionally just to avoid it or duplicate service configuration unnecessarily.

Validate baseline and latest check graphs in cloud, including after explicit realization of all suites/targets, not only a lazy dry-run. Verify the selected default and ControllerTelemetry task names, the absence of unselected tasks from check, and the shared service assignment for manual baseline vaadinLatestTest and both latest tasks. Apply narrow formatting and use focused configuration checks rather than running frontend/Selenium tests merely to inspect the task graph. Preserve dependency versions, metadata flags, suite classpaths, all unrelated files, the existing prerequisite/base branch, and draft state. Do not modify the execution DSL, agent instructions, conventions documentation, or other PRs. Do not create a new PR or reply to review comments.

